# Build context sent to the daemon. Without this file `COPY . .` ships the whole
# working tree — 14 GB of target/ locally, and any .env sitting next to it.
#
# The .env exclusion is the important one. The production stage copies only the
# compiled binary, so a secret in the builder never reaches the shipped image —
# but deploy.yml exports every layer with `cache-to: type=gha,mode=max`, so a
# JWT_SECRET or RESEND_API_KEY copied into the builder would land in the shared
# Actions cache.

target/
.git/
.github/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local object-storage backend and container state
data/
docker/postgres/data/
docker/valkey/data/

# Not needed to build
*.md
!README.md
